WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.390
In October 2009, the US
unemployment rate hit 10 percent.

2
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.050
Less than two years earlier,

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.970
it had been 5 percent.

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.660
Recessions push unemployment up.

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.900
But the rate never falls to zero,

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.800
not even in the best years.

7
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.020
So why are some people out of work even

8
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.030
when the economy is booming?

9
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:24.840
In this mission, you'll meet the three
types of unemployment that economists use.

10
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.050
Then you'll split an
unemployment rate into its parts,

11
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.920
and find the natural rate of unemployment.

12
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.060
Your mission: find out
why there are always some

13
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.910
people out of work, even
in the best of times.
